# rena0-hit-ground-300 — F1-3 fixture
# Placement mirrors the device-free melee tests (tests/damage_scale_test.cpp:184-185,
# tests/fighter_script_test.cpp:761): the dummy is kept on the attacker's posed attack
# volume with test::Combo::placeAtAttack, rather than placed by an invented sphere.
# Damage is the recovered 8 HP per landed melee hit (tests/damage_scale_test.cpp:195,
# FUN_00639160).
#
# Measured on this build with the dummy on the volume: the swing is active over updates
# 14-19 and the contact lands at update 15 (100 -> 92 HP). Note this window differs from
# the same row's window with the dummy out of reach, which opens at 25+ — see
# rena0-melee-ground-300.fixture and the open question recorded with it.
# Body separation off: this fixture keeps the dummy on the posed attack volume (35-50 units
# away), a placement inside FUN_006394c0's 60-unit radius that the original never allows. With
# separation on the contact lands a tick earlier and the recorded tick no longer holds. The
# realistic-spacing re-record is V3-45's open item.
body_separation 0
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 300
collision open-field
input 0 MELEE
place_at_attack active
expect 14 melee_active 1
expect 15 melee_hit 1
expect 16 dummy_hp 92
expect 15 melee_victim 1
expect 15 swing_hits 1
expect 15 dummy_alive 1
expect 22 melee_recovery 1
